WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.083 --> 00:00:01.877
I actually don't care about anything else.

00:00:01.877 --> 00:00:06.583
Speed both in people skills and hard work will trump anything.

00:00:06.583 --> 00:00:10.180
("99" by Russ ft. Totem &amp;amp; Paulina)

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:17.000
(heart monitor beeping)

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.260
Speed is four billion times more important than perfection.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:23.273
Speed.

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:26.761
When you're not spending any time worrying,

00:00:26.761 --> 00:00:28.721
your spending time on executing.

00:00:28.721 --> 00:00:30.530
That's what a great culture is.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.490
It's speed.

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.034
You're not spending the 15 minutes a day bickering.

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:37.059
You're not spending the four hours a day wondering if that

00:00:37.059 --> 00:00:38.912
person trying to ruin you.

00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:53.120
I understand it's a race and yet speed is a variable for success

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:54.794
to me in a big way.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.640
Hustle, patience and speed are very much rubbing against each

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.220
other but it's like the diamond comes from that.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.980
On your day-to-day work,

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.280
you have to be fast with the clients.

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.940
They email you, you email them back.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.960
Like your day-to-day but your vision,

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.180
what you want to achieve in life you're not gonna build it in

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.020
one year and so many people have it reversed.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.580
In the day-to-day they're slow and in the macro they want their

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.520
business to be huge the next day.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.000
People talk a big game.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.880
"GaryVee, you're gonna buy the Jets,

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:36.300
"I'm gonna buy the Rams."

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.300
Yo, bro, nobody, nobody unless they were a trust fund baby ever

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.960
bought the Rams when they go skiing

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.980
for a week when they're 24.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.140
I am massively, at a global level patient but on a

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.680
practical level and an execution level, I'm very fast.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.620
It really is religion and church.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.780
When you align on religion you can go fast and speed is such a

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:11.320
bigger aspect of business than people realize and so instead of

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.340
jockeying and politicking and pondering and posturing and

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.740
debating for three or four months,

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:17.300
we're just in do mode now

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:18.300
and when you're in do mode

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.620
you fucking get shit done.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:30.140
So I just went on a huge email storm I guess,

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.280
email rant to the whole company.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.360
It was great.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.520
It was huge communication thing about the inefficiencies.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.280
I just got a lot done in an hour and a half on email that will

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.780
impact our company for a long time.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:52.140
I think it's crazy when Goliath loses to David.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.740
Goliath should never lose to David.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.640
That means bad strategy.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.440
If we're David 'cause it's us versus WPP,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.780
get a fucking rock and put it in his fucking eye.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.880
If you don't give a fuck about what people think,

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:03.640
you can do everything.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.180
The reality is I think speed trumps so much

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.440
that I'm blown away by people that get caught up in this

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.960
and really it just leads to you being

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:15.920
disproportionately not successful

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.780
because you're too slow.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.340
You're overthinking things.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.880
Speed is the only thing that matters,

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:26.140
and opinions predicated on people's insecurities and ego

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.120
slows shit down.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:53.000
("99" by Russ ft. Totem &amp;amp; Paulina)

